  "full_target": "Let n,m be positive integers, u:R^n×(0,∞)→R^m jointly smooth and q a unit vector. Assume |u|=1, u_tt−Δ_xu=a u, and u=q outside compact spatial sets uniformly on compact time intervals. Define e=|u_t|²+Σ|∂_xj u|² and E=∫e dx. Prove e integrable, E differentiable, E'=0 for all r>0.",
  "conclusion": "For every r>0, e(·,r) is Lebesgue integrable, E is differentiable at r, and E'(r)=0.",
